#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Located in the plugin folder: docs/user-guide.md — installation, setup and translation from start to finish."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Fill in a row for each language, choose the default language — the one you write in — and save."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Be sure to check two things:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "\"WordPress locale\" is NOT the language code. The code (bg) goes into the page address; the locale (bg_BG) is the name under which WordPress stores translations of its own interface. For English it can be either en_US or en_GB."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "The language pack. If it says \"no pack\", click \"Download\". Without it WordPress shows the English originals of all labels, and it looks as if the plugin does not work."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "To check: open a site page with the language prefix. The menu and comment form should be translated on their own, without any effort on your part."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
#: src/Frontend/LanguageSwitcherWidget.php
#: src/Frontend/NavMenu.php
msgid "Language switcher"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Three ways, take your pick:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "\"Appearance → Menus\", the \"Languages\" box: tick \"Dropdown\" or \"Inline\" and add it to the menu. One item is enough — the plugin builds all the languages under it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "The [mlp_language_switcher] shortcode in the text."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "The \"Language switcher\" widget."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Language order"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "follows the order of rows in the table: rearrange them with the arrows in the first column and save. The default language can be moved too — it does not have to be first."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "What the visitor sees"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "is chosen below the table: language name, code (RU, EN), flag only, or flag with code. Flags have their own tab in this help."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "In \"Dropdown\" mode, the item that opens it shows the current language in the same form, not its own menu label. This way the visitor can see which language the page is in before opening the list."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Flags"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Upload a flag right here: in the \"Flag\" column click \"Choose file\" in the right row and save. The file name does not matter — the plugin saves it under the language code from the first column."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Where to get them: %s is a ready-made set of all flags (MIT license). The ones you need are in the flags/4x3 folder; you do not have to download the whole set: open the file you need and save it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Which file to take:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "in flag sets the files are named by country, not by language. Russian and Bulgarian correspond to ru and bg, and English to gb (United Kingdom) or us (United States), your choice. There is no need to rename anything: the plugin saves the file under the right name itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Only SVG up to 64 KB is accepted. The uploaded file is stripped of scripts: an SVG is not just an image, it can contain executable code, and without cleaning it would run on your domain for anyone who opened the file link. This is why WordPress does not allow SVG uploads without a plugin."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "To remove an image, tick \"remove\" next to it and save."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "No image: the plugin shows the emoji from the same field, and if that is empty too, the language code. The switcher is never left blank."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Why an image and not an emoji: Windows cannot draw emoji flags at all — instead of a flag the visitor sees two letters. On a MacBook or phone everything looks fine, so the problem is easy to miss."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "In the dropdown the flag is always text: HTML itself does not allow an image inside it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "AI translation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Without an OpenAI key there are simply no \"Translate with AI\" buttons — everything else works as usual."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "The plugin never translates on its own and never contacts OpenAI in the background: only when you click a button. The daily character limit caps spending, and a translation that is already saved is not paid for again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Which tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Rule: if you wrote it yourself, it is \"Content\"; if you did not, it is \"Interface\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "\"Content\" is article text, headings, menu items, image captions. This is yours, and it is the main tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "\"Interface\" is \"Reply\", \"Leave a comment\", cart buttons. WordPress, the theme and plugins draw these; almost all of it is translated automatically from the language pack."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "\"SEO/GEO\" is what is not visible on the page: the description for Google and the preview when a link is sent in a messenger."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "How to search"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Without special characters the search looks for the whole phrase, but not as part of another word: \"AI\" will find \"AI Act\" but not \"domain\" — the letters there match only by chance."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "An asterisk (*) stands for any number of any characters, as in Windows file search or Spotlight on Mac:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "*blog/en/ — the string ENDS with \"blog/en/\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "blog/en/* — the string STARTS with \"blog/en/\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "*plugin* — \"plugin\" anywhere, including inside another word (for example \"plugins\") — without asterisks it would not be found."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "It searches both the source and the translation. On the \"Links\" tab this is the most reliable way to find a specific address: without asterisks the search also finds anything that merely contains the phrase somewhere in the middle of the path."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "What to translate and what not"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "On the \"Interface\" tab, look at the \"Source\" column:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "\"Theme: …\" — translate these first. This is what the visitor sees on every page."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Shop plugin — translate it if you sell: an English button in the storefront hurts sales."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Rank Math, Akismet and other admin-side plugins — do not touch them at all. Their labels are visible only to you; a visitor never sees them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Your translation always takes priority over the official one. \"Reset to official\" restores the version from the language pack."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "If something is wrong"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "The text is on the site but not in the list."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Most often the page simply has not been opened in this language — the list fills only after a page is displayed. If it has been opened: the text may be in a \"Preformatted\" block — the plugin deliberately leaves such blocks alone, as they usually hold code. Replace it with a regular paragraph."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Half of the form is translated and half is not."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "The WordPress language pack translated what WordPress draws, but the theme replaced some labels with its own, and there is no theme translation for your language. Look for them on the \"Interface\" tab, source: your theme."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "The list is cluttered."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "The \"Clear untranslated strings\" button at the bottom removes discovered strings that nobody translated. It does not touch translated ones, and anything needed will be collected again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "The translation is saved but the site shows the old text."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Clear the page cache — the caching plugin is serving a saved copy."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "How to translate"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Choose a language, enter the page address and click \"Open\". Then there are two ways:"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "\"Translate the whole post with AI\" — title, excerpt and full text in one operation. The \"Empty segments only\" mode does not touch what is already translated."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Click the text directly in the preview — a field for that string opens on the left."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "Nothing is saved automatically: until you click \"Save\", the translation remains a draft."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
msgid "If the layout gets in the way"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/HelpTabs.php
